1
00:00:02,717 --> 00:00:04,385
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:05,136 --> 00:00:06,471
Earth.

3
00:00:07,013 --> 00:00:08,473
Fire.

4
00:00:09,182 --> 00:00:10,642
Air.

5
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:15,605
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,688 --> 00:00:19,192
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:20,026 --> 00:00:22,946
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:23,029 --> 00:00:24,072
could stop them.

9
00:00:24,155 --> 00:00:27,200
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,534 --> 00:00:28,785
A hundred years passed,

11
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:31,329
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

12
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:33,081
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,164 --> 00:00:35,291
And although
his airbending skills are great,

14
00:00:35,416 --> 00:00:38,002
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:38,086 --> 00:00:39,087
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:42,298
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:00:48,221 --> 00:00:50,723
ROKU: Previously on Avatar...

18
00:00:50,848 --> 00:00:52,058
KATARA: Appa is missing.

19
00:00:52,183 --> 00:00:54,352
We hope to find him in Ba Sing Se.

20
00:00:54,727 --> 00:00:58,147
Professor Zei, head of anthropology
at Ba Sing Se University.

21
00:00:58,523 --> 00:01:02,235
This library is said to contain
a vast collection of knowledge.

22
00:01:04,195 --> 00:01:07,448
SOKKA: Firebenders lose their
bending during a solar eclipse!

23
00:01:07,532 --> 00:01:10,618
We've gotta get this information
to the Earth King at Ba Sing Se.

24
00:01:13,621 --> 00:01:14,831
Hey!

25
00:01:14,956 --> 00:01:17,166
What are you doing firebending your tea?

26
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:20,044
So the old guy had some hot tea, big deal.

27
00:01:20,169 --> 00:01:21,629
He heated it himself.

28
00:01:21,754 --> 00:01:23,923
Those guys are firebenders.

29
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:45,111
Look, the inner wall.

30
00:01:48,406 --> 00:01:51,618
I can't believe we finally made it
to Ba Sing Se in one piece.

31
00:01:51,701 --> 00:01:52,785
Hey, don't jinx it!

32
00:01:52,869 --> 00:01:56,497
We could still be attacked by some
giant, exploding Fire Nation spoon.

33
00:01:56,581 --> 00:02:00,043
Or find out the city's been submerged
in an ocean full of killer shrimp.

34
00:02:00,126 --> 00:02:02,253
You been hitting the cactus juice again?

35
00:02:02,337 --> 00:02:03,338
I'm just sayin'.

36
00:02:03,421 --> 00:02:04,922
Weird stuff happens to us.

37
00:02:08,217 --> 00:02:09,719
( SUCKING )

38
00:02:11,554 --> 00:02:13,723
Don't worry, Aang, we'll find Appa.

39
00:02:13,806 --> 00:02:15,391
It's such a big city.

40
00:02:15,475 --> 00:02:16,893
He's a giant bison.

41
00:02:16,976 --> 00:02:18,811
Where could someone possibly hide him?

42
00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:28,071
Oh.

43
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:41,918
TOPH: Ah, back in the city.

44
00:02:42,001 --> 00:02:43,002
Great.

45
00:02:43,086 --> 00:02:45,296
SOKKA: What's the problem? It's amazing!

46
00:02:45,755 --> 00:02:47,882
Just a bunch of walls and rules.

47
00:02:48,424 --> 00:02:50,885
You wait, you'll get sick of it
in a couple of days.

48
00:02:56,516 --> 00:02:58,476
AANG: I'm comin' for you, buddy.

49
00:02:59,894 --> 00:03:01,479
He's here, I can feel it.

50
00:03:10,196 --> 00:03:12,990
Hello, my name is Joo Dee.

51
00:03:13,074 --> 00:03:17,453
I have been given the great honor
of showing the Avatar around Ba Sing Se.

52
00:03:17,537 --> 00:03:20,373
And you must be Sokka, Katara and Toph.

53
00:03:20,915 --> 00:03:22,709
Welcome to our wonderful city.

54
00:03:22,792 --> 00:03:24,293
Shall we get started?

55
00:03:24,585 --> 00:03:27,296
Yes, we have information
about the Fire Nation army

56
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,924
that we need to deliver
to the Earth King immediately.

57
00:03:30,007 --> 00:03:32,135
Great, let's begin our tour.

58
00:03:32,218 --> 00:03:34,804
And then I'll show you
to your new home, here.

59
00:03:34,887 --> 00:03:36,597
I think you'll like it.

60
00:03:37,348 --> 00:03:38,558
Augh!

61
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:40,768
Maybe you missed what I said.

62
00:03:40,852 --> 00:03:43,604
We need to talk to the king
about the war, it's important.

63
00:03:43,896 --> 00:03:45,523
You're in Ba Sing Se, now.

64
00:03:45,606 --> 00:03:47,108
Everyone is safe here.

65
00:03:51,988 --> 00:03:53,740
This is the lower ring.

66
00:03:53,823 --> 00:03:55,491
What's that wall for?

67
00:03:55,575 --> 00:03:58,077
Oh, Ba Sing Se has many walls.

68
00:03:58,161 --> 00:04:00,413
There are the ones outside, protecting us,

69
00:04:00,538 --> 00:04:03,624
and the ones inside,
that help maintain order.

70
00:04:03,958 --> 00:04:06,419
This is where our newest arrivals live,

71
00:04:06,502 --> 00:04:10,465
as well as our craftsmen and artisans,
people that work with their hands.

72
00:04:10,965 --> 00:04:12,842
It's so quaint and lively.

73
00:04:15,386 --> 00:04:17,388
You do want to watch your step, though.

74
00:04:17,472 --> 00:04:21,017
Why do they have all these poor people
blocked off in one part of the city?

75
00:04:21,350 --> 00:04:23,770
This is why I never came here before.

76
00:04:23,853 --> 00:04:27,440
I always heard it was so different
from the way the monks taught us to live.

77
00:04:36,449 --> 00:04:42,455
I just want our new place to look nice
in case someone brings home a lady friend.

78
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:44,165
This city is a prison.

79
00:04:44,248 --> 00:04:46,083
I don't want to make a life here.

80
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:50,213
IROH: Life happens wherever you are,
whether you make it or not.

81
00:04:50,296 --> 00:04:55,343
Now come on, I found us some new jobs
and we start this afternoon.

82
00:04:57,970 --> 00:05:01,349
Look at them, firebenders living
right under everyone's nose.

83
00:05:03,476 --> 00:05:06,103
SMELLERBEE: Jet, you saw a man
with a hot cup of tea.

84
00:05:06,187 --> 00:05:07,939
It doesn't prove he's a firebender.

85
00:05:08,022 --> 00:05:11,150
And what if he is,
are we supposed to attack them?

86
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:14,362
I thought we were starting over here,
changing our ways.

87
00:05:15,112 --> 00:05:18,491
We are. When I get the evidence I need,
I'll report them to the police

88
00:05:18,574 --> 00:05:21,035
and let them handle it, okay?

89
00:05:23,412 --> 00:05:26,082
JOO DEE: This is the middle ring
of Ba Sing Se,

90
00:05:26,165 --> 00:05:29,961
Home to the financial district,
shops and restaurants and the University.

91
00:05:30,044 --> 00:05:32,505
Yeah, we met a professor
from Ba Sing Se University.

92
00:05:32,588 --> 00:05:34,674
He took us to
an ancient underground library

93
00:05:34,757 --> 00:05:36,884
where we discovered information
about the war

94
00:05:36,968 --> 00:05:39,220
that is absolutely crucial
for the king to hear!

95
00:05:39,303 --> 00:05:41,305
Isn't history fascinating?

96
00:05:41,389 --> 00:05:45,810
Look, here's one of the oldest buildings
in the middle ring, town hall.

97
00:05:47,019 --> 00:05:48,229
Is that woman deaf?

98
00:05:48,312 --> 00:05:50,481
She only seems to hear
every other word I say.

99
00:05:50,565 --> 00:05:52,275
It's called being handled.

100
00:05:52,358 --> 00:05:53,651
Get used to it.

101
00:06:01,909 --> 00:06:04,996
Well, you certainly look like
official tea servers.

102
00:06:05,413 --> 00:06:06,581
How do you feel?

103
00:06:06,664 --> 00:06:07,874
Ridiculous.

104
00:06:07,957 --> 00:06:11,669
Uh, does this possibly come
in a larger size?

105
00:06:12,086 --> 00:06:14,088
I have extra string in the back.

106
00:06:14,171 --> 00:06:16,215
Have some tea while you wait.

107
00:06:20,678 --> 00:06:22,054
Eow!

108
00:06:22,388 --> 00:06:25,850
This tea is nothing more
than hot leaf juice!

109
00:06:25,933 --> 00:06:28,644
Uncle, that's what all tea is.

110
00:06:28,728 --> 00:06:33,524
How could a member of my own family
say something so horrible?

111
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:36,777
We'll have to make some
major changes around here.

112
00:06:37,194 --> 00:06:38,195
( GASPING )

113
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:47,330
JOO DEE: The upper ring is home
to our most important citizens.

114
00:06:47,413 --> 00:06:49,415
Your house is not too far from here.

115
00:06:53,586 --> 00:06:55,212
What's inside that wall?

116
00:06:58,341 --> 00:07:00,843
And who are
the mean-looking guys in robes?

117
00:07:00,927 --> 00:07:03,012
Inside is the royal palace.

118
00:07:03,095 --> 00:07:07,725
Those men are agents of the Dai Li,
the cultural authority of Ba Sing Se.

119
00:07:07,808 --> 00:07:10,227
They are the guardians
of all our traditions.

120
00:07:10,853 --> 00:07:12,021
Can we see the king now?

121
00:07:12,355 --> 00:07:13,564
( LAUGHING ) Oh, no!

122
00:07:13,648 --> 00:07:16,442
One doesn't just pop in on the Earth King.

123
00:07:19,528 --> 00:07:21,948
Here we are, your new home.

124
00:07:25,451 --> 00:07:26,827
More good news.

125
00:07:26,911 --> 00:07:30,623
Your request for an audience
with the Earth King is being processed,

126
00:07:30,748 --> 00:07:33,501
and should be put through
in about a month.

127
00:07:33,584 --> 00:07:35,252
Much more quickly than usual.

128
00:07:35,628 --> 00:07:36,879
A month?

129
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:40,257
Six to eight weeks, actually.

130
00:07:47,264 --> 00:07:48,432
Isn't it nice?

131
00:07:48,849 --> 00:07:51,102
I think you'll really enjoy it here.

132
00:07:51,185 --> 00:07:53,896
I think we'd enjoy it more
if we weren't staying so long.

133
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:55,606
Can't we see the king any sooner?

134
00:07:55,690 --> 00:07:59,235
The Earth King is very busy
running the finest city in the world,

135
00:07:59,318 --> 00:08:01,404
but he will see you
as soon as time permits.

136
00:08:02,071 --> 00:08:05,866
If we're gonna be here for a month,
we should spend our time looking for Appa.

137
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:08,869
I'll be happy to escort you
anywhere you'd like to go.

138
00:08:09,161 --> 00:08:10,705
We don't need a babysitter.

139
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:13,207
Oh, I won't get in the way.

140
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:16,293
And to leave you alone
would make me a bad host.

141
00:08:16,377 --> 00:08:18,629
Where shall we start?

142
00:08:21,924 --> 00:08:23,217
( CHIRPING )

143
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,302
( SCREECHING )

144
00:08:25,386 --> 00:08:28,514
I'm sorry, but I haven't heard
anything about a flying bison.

145
00:08:28,806 --> 00:08:30,641
I didn't even know there were any.

146
00:08:30,725 --> 00:08:33,811
If someone wanted to sell a stolen animal
without anyone knowing,

147
00:08:33,894 --> 00:08:34,895
where would they go?

148
00:08:34,979 --> 00:08:36,188
Where's the black market?

149
00:08:36,272 --> 00:08:38,357
Who runs it? Come on, you know.

150
00:08:39,191 --> 00:08:40,234
Uh...

151
00:08:43,487 --> 00:08:46,198
That would be illegal.

152
00:08:46,282 --> 00:08:47,491
You'll have to leave now.

153
00:08:47,575 --> 00:08:49,493
Your lemur is harassing my sparrowkeets.

154
00:08:54,373 --> 00:08:58,419
STUDENT: Hmm, I've never seen
any sandbenders or nomads around here.

155
00:08:58,502 --> 00:09:01,922
You should ask Professor Zei,
he teaches the class on desert cultures.

156
00:09:02,006 --> 00:09:03,549
Right.

157
00:09:03,632 --> 00:09:07,303
And which of your professors could we ask
about the war with the Fire Nation?

158
00:09:10,222 --> 00:09:14,477
I don't know, I'm not a political science
student, I have to get to class.

159
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,853
Unh!

160
00:09:19,857 --> 00:09:23,027
JOO DEE: Well, I'm sorry no one
has seen your bison.

161
00:09:23,152 --> 00:09:24,862
Why don't you go get some rest?

162
00:09:24,945 --> 00:09:26,822
Someone will be over with dinner later.

163
00:09:34,205 --> 00:09:35,331
Hey, come with me.

164
00:09:40,961 --> 00:09:42,797
You're the Avatar.

165
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:44,840
I heard you were in town.

166
00:09:44,924 --> 00:09:46,258
I'm Pong.

167
00:09:46,342 --> 00:09:47,676
Nice to meet you, Pong.

168
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,970
So, Pong, what's goin' on with this city?

169
00:09:50,054 --> 00:09:52,598
Why is everyone here
so scared to talk about the war?

170
00:09:52,681 --> 00:09:54,433
War, scared?

171
00:09:54,517 --> 00:09:55,684
What do you mean?

172
00:09:55,768 --> 00:09:57,686
I can feel you shaking.

173
00:09:57,770 --> 00:10:00,397
Look, I'm just
a minor government official.

174
00:10:00,481 --> 00:10:02,900
I've waited three years to get this house.

175
00:10:03,526 --> 00:10:05,111
I don't want to get into trouble.

176
00:10:05,611 --> 00:10:07,238
Get in trouble with who?

177
00:10:07,321 --> 00:10:10,491
Shh, listen, you can't
mention the war, here.

178
00:10:10,574 --> 00:10:13,953
And whatever you do,
stay away from the Dai Li.

179
00:10:20,668 --> 00:10:22,795
IROH: Would you like a pot of tea?

180
00:10:22,878 --> 00:10:25,840
ZUKO: We've been working
in a tea shop all day.

181
00:10:25,965 --> 00:10:27,550
I'm sick of tea.

182
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:29,593
Sick of tea?

183
00:10:29,677 --> 00:10:32,304
That's like being sick of breathing.

184
00:10:33,722 --> 00:10:37,017
Have you seen our spark rocks
to heat up the water?

185
00:10:37,101 --> 00:10:39,520
They're not there.

186
00:10:39,603 --> 00:10:42,022
You'll have to firebend, old man.

187
00:10:43,941 --> 00:10:45,693
JET: Where are you going?

188
00:10:46,235 --> 00:10:49,280
IROH: I borrowed our neighbor's.

189
00:10:49,363 --> 00:10:50,823
Such kind people.

190
00:10:55,911 --> 00:10:57,788
( CHIRPING )

191
00:11:00,249 --> 00:11:02,626
( YAWNING )

192
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:05,671
( GASPING )

193
00:11:05,963 --> 00:11:06,964
I've got it!

194
00:11:07,047 --> 00:11:09,049
I know how we're gonna see the Earth King.

195
00:11:09,383 --> 00:11:10,843
How're we supposed to do that?

196
00:11:10,926 --> 00:11:13,679
"One doesn't just pop in
on the Earth King."

197
00:11:13,929 --> 00:11:17,224
The king is having a party
at the palace tonight for his pet bear.

198
00:11:17,308 --> 00:11:19,101
You mean platypus-bear?

199
00:11:19,185 --> 00:11:21,145
No, it just says "bear."

200
00:11:21,645 --> 00:11:23,772
Certainly you mean his pet skunk-bear.

201
00:11:23,856 --> 00:11:25,232
Or his armadillo-bear.

202
00:11:25,316 --> 00:11:26,567
Gopher-bear?

203
00:11:26,650 --> 00:11:28,485
Just "bear."

204
00:11:29,403 --> 00:11:31,572
This place is weird.

205
00:11:31,739 --> 00:11:33,282
The palace will be packed.

206
00:11:33,365 --> 00:11:35,201
We can sneak in with a crowd.

207
00:11:35,284 --> 00:11:36,994
- Won't work.
- Why not?

208
00:11:37,077 --> 00:11:39,205
Well, no offense
to you simple country folk,

209
00:11:39,288 --> 00:11:42,583
but a real society crowd
would spot you a mile away.

210
00:11:42,666 --> 00:11:44,001
You've got no manners.

211
00:11:44,668 --> 00:11:46,212
Excuse me?

212
00:11:46,295 --> 00:11:47,755
I've got no manners?

213
00:11:47,838 --> 00:11:50,507
You're not exactly Lady Fancy Fingers.

214
00:11:50,966 --> 00:11:52,092
( TOPH BURPS )

215
00:11:52,176 --> 00:11:55,638
I learned proper society
behavior and chose to leave it.

216
00:11:55,721 --> 00:11:57,431
You never learned anything.

217
00:11:57,806 --> 00:12:00,142
And frankly, it's a little too late.

218
00:12:00,226 --> 00:12:01,852
Ah-ha, but you learned it!

219
00:12:01,936 --> 00:12:03,187
You could teach us.

220
00:12:03,270 --> 00:12:05,022
Yeah, I'm mastering every element.

221
00:12:05,105 --> 00:12:06,357
How hard can manners be?

222
00:12:07,399 --> 00:12:09,777
"Good evening, Mr. Sokka Water Tribe.

223
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:11,820
"Miss Katara Water Tribe.

224
00:12:11,904 --> 00:12:16,200
"Lord Momo of the Momo dynasty,
your Momo-ness."

225
00:12:16,283 --> 00:12:19,578
"Avatar Aang, how you do go on."

226
00:12:23,874 --> 00:12:24,875
AANG: Ow!

227
00:12:25,125 --> 00:12:27,127
Katara might be able to pull it off,

228
00:12:27,211 --> 00:12:29,797
but you two would be lucky
to pass as busboys.

229
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:31,715
But I feel so fancy.

230
00:12:35,552 --> 00:12:36,720
AANG: Earth!
SOKKA: Fire!

231
00:12:37,513 --> 00:12:38,806
Augh.

232
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,641
Ooh.

233
00:12:44,645 --> 00:12:45,813
( GIGGLING )

234
00:12:46,355 --> 00:12:48,691
Wow, you look beautiful.

235
00:12:50,109 --> 00:12:51,944
Don't talk to the commoners, Katara.

236
00:12:52,027 --> 00:12:53,696
First rule of society.

237
00:12:54,113 --> 00:12:57,866
We'll get in the party and then find
a way to let you in through the side gate.

238
00:13:00,995 --> 00:13:02,496
( GONG RINGING )

239
00:13:12,798 --> 00:13:14,591
SMELLERBEE: Jet, we need to talk.

240
00:13:14,675 --> 00:13:16,719
What? Oh, great, it's you guys.

241
00:13:16,802 --> 00:13:19,930
Where have you been? I could use
some help with surveillance here.

242
00:13:20,014 --> 00:13:23,809
We've been talking, and we think
you're becoming obsessed with this.

243
00:13:23,892 --> 00:13:25,102
It's not healthy.

244
00:13:25,185 --> 00:13:26,312
Oh, really?

245
00:13:26,395 --> 00:13:27,521
You both think this?

246
00:13:28,731 --> 00:13:31,066
We came here to make a fresh start.

247
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,776
But you won't let this go.

248
00:13:32,860 --> 00:13:34,486
Even though there's no real proof!

249
00:13:34,570 --> 00:13:36,238
Well, maybe if you'd help me.

250
00:13:36,322 --> 00:13:38,157
Jet, you've gotta stop this.

251
00:13:38,574 --> 00:13:40,868
Maybe you've forgotten why we
need to start over.

252
00:13:40,951 --> 00:13:44,288
Maybe you've forgotten about how
the Fire Nation left us all homeless?

253
00:13:44,371 --> 00:13:46,540
How they wiped out
all the people we loved?

254
00:13:46,623 --> 00:13:49,460
If you don't wanna help me,
I'll get the evidence on my own.

255
00:13:57,384 --> 00:13:59,511
This is the best tea in the city.

256
00:13:59,970 --> 00:14:03,015
The secret ingredient is love.

257
00:14:08,187 --> 00:14:10,064
I think you're due for a raise.

258
00:14:12,941 --> 00:14:14,193
I'm tired of waiting.

259
00:14:14,276 --> 00:14:16,695
These two men are firebenders!

260
00:14:26,663 --> 00:14:28,207
I know they're firebenders!

261
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:30,376
I saw the old man heating his tea.

262
00:14:30,959 --> 00:14:32,461
He works in a tea shop.

263
00:14:32,669 --> 00:14:34,755
He's a firebender, I'm telling you!

264
00:14:35,172 --> 00:14:37,800
Drop your swords, boy, nice and easy.

265
00:14:37,883 --> 00:14:39,385
You'll have to defend yourself.

266
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,220
Then everyone will know.

267
00:14:41,512 --> 00:14:43,680
Go ahead, show them what you can do.

268
00:14:45,307 --> 00:14:46,392
You want a show?

269
00:14:46,475 --> 00:14:47,476
I'll give you a show.

270
00:15:08,747 --> 00:15:09,998
MAN: Invitation, please.

271
00:15:10,082 --> 00:15:11,542
I think this will do.

272
00:15:12,084 --> 00:15:14,002
No entry without an invitation.

273
00:15:14,086 --> 00:15:15,629
Step out of line, please.

274
00:15:16,171 --> 00:15:19,967
Look, the Pangs and the Yumsoon-Hans
are waiting in there for us.

275
00:15:20,050 --> 00:15:22,761
I'm gonna have to
tell them who didn't let me in.

276
00:15:22,845 --> 00:15:24,430
Step out of line, please.

277
00:15:34,356 --> 00:15:35,399
KATARA: Sir?

278
00:15:35,482 --> 00:15:38,944
I'm sorry to bother you, but my
cousin lost our invitations.

279
00:15:39,528 --> 00:15:40,946
( WHISPERING ) She's blind.

280
00:15:41,363 --> 00:15:42,865
Do you think you could help us?

281
00:15:42,948 --> 00:15:45,784
Our family's inside,
and I'm sure they're very worried.

282
00:15:46,535 --> 00:15:47,578
I am honored.

283
00:15:47,786 --> 00:15:49,121
Please come with me.

284
00:15:55,836 --> 00:15:57,045
Nyaa. ( BLOWING RASPBERRY )

285
00:16:01,425 --> 00:16:03,093
He's taking all the good stuff.

286
00:16:03,469 --> 00:16:07,264
Quiet, you don't know what I had to do
to get seats this near the bear.

287
00:16:13,562 --> 00:16:14,813
It's beautiful, isn't it?

288
00:16:15,314 --> 00:16:17,483
By the way, I'm Long Feng.

289
00:16:17,566 --> 00:16:19,401
I'm a cultural minister to the king.

290
00:16:19,860 --> 00:16:23,322
I'm Hwamei, and this is Dung.

291
00:16:23,906 --> 00:16:24,907
Ow!

292
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,533
Now where is your family?

293
00:16:26,617 --> 00:16:28,076
I'd love to meet them.

294
00:16:28,368 --> 00:16:31,747
Uh, I don't see 'em right now,
but I'm sure we'll find them soon.

295
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:33,290
Thanks for all your help.

296
00:16:37,252 --> 00:16:38,754
Don't worry, as your escort,

297
00:16:38,837 --> 00:16:43,050
it would be dishonorable to abandon you
ladies without finding your family, first.

298
00:16:43,133 --> 00:16:44,510
We'll keep looking.

299
00:16:47,346 --> 00:16:48,764
Where are they?

300
00:16:48,847 --> 00:16:51,099
Look, I came up with a back-up plan.

301
00:16:51,183 --> 00:16:53,769
We dress Momo like a ghost, okay?

302
00:16:53,852 --> 00:16:56,563
He flies by the guards,
creating a distraction.

303
00:16:56,647 --> 00:16:59,149
Then we blast a hole in the wall...

304
00:16:59,233 --> 00:17:01,485
Or we can go in with these guys.

305
00:17:01,568 --> 00:17:03,570
AANG: Toph said we might pass as busboys.

306
00:17:04,112 --> 00:17:06,573
Okay, but remember that Momo ghost plan.

307
00:17:06,657 --> 00:17:07,950
I think it's a winner.

308
00:17:09,993 --> 00:17:11,537
Ugh!

309
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:12,746
( GRUNTING )

310
00:17:13,205 --> 00:17:15,457
You must be getting tired
of using those swords.

311
00:17:15,541 --> 00:17:18,168
Why don't you go ahead and firebend at me?

312
00:17:18,252 --> 00:17:20,170
Please, son, you're confused!

313
00:17:20,254 --> 00:17:22,130
You don't know what you're doing!

314
00:17:22,923 --> 00:17:26,301
JET: Bet you wish he helped you out
with a little fire blast right now.

315
00:17:27,594 --> 00:17:29,471
You're the one who needs help.

316
00:17:39,064 --> 00:17:41,608
You see that?
The Fire Nation is trying to silence me!

317
00:17:41,984 --> 00:17:43,485
It'll never happen.

318
00:17:44,069 --> 00:17:45,070
( GRUNTING )

319
00:17:49,825 --> 00:17:51,285
Where are Toph and Katara?

320
00:17:51,368 --> 00:17:54,037
Forget about them, just keep
an eye out for the king.

321
00:17:54,746 --> 00:17:56,498
I don't know what he looks like.

322
00:17:56,582 --> 00:18:00,669
You know, royal,
flowing robe, fancy jewelry.

323
00:18:02,129 --> 00:18:03,672
AANG: That could be anyone.

324
00:18:04,214 --> 00:18:06,049
Another crab puff, please.

325
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,176
You found us!

326
00:18:08,260 --> 00:18:11,179
I'd know your little footsteps
anywhere, twinkle toes.

327
00:18:11,263 --> 00:18:12,889
Thanks for letting us in.

328
00:18:12,973 --> 00:18:16,310
Sorry, but the guy who escorted us in
won't let us out of his sight.

329
00:18:16,727 --> 00:18:17,894
What guy?

330
00:18:19,354 --> 00:18:20,897
What are you doing here?

331
00:18:21,189 --> 00:18:24,818
You have to leave immediately,
or we'll all be in terrible trouble.

332
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:26,820
Not until we see the king.

333
00:18:27,279 --> 00:18:29,197
You don't understand. You must go.

334
00:18:31,116 --> 00:18:32,784
( WOMAN SCREAMING )

335
00:18:32,868 --> 00:18:33,952
Oh!

336
00:18:34,036 --> 00:18:35,662
AANG: Sorry, no, don't shout.

337
00:18:41,168 --> 00:18:42,294
The Avatar.

338
00:18:42,628 --> 00:18:45,213
Oh, I didn't know
the Avatar would be here.

339
00:18:53,221 --> 00:18:54,431
( LAUGHING WEAKLY )

340
00:18:54,514 --> 00:18:56,933
You keep their attention
while I look for the king.

341
00:18:57,017 --> 00:18:58,435
Watch this, everybody.

342
00:19:07,861 --> 00:19:09,363
CROWD: Ooh...

343
00:19:09,446 --> 00:19:10,572
( APPLAUSE )

344
00:19:11,031 --> 00:19:12,115
( LAUGHING, GROWLING )

345
00:19:12,658 --> 00:19:13,659
( GRUNTING )

346
00:19:22,709 --> 00:19:24,336
Drop your weapons.

347
00:19:24,419 --> 00:19:26,129
Arrest them, they're firebenders.

348
00:19:26,880 --> 00:19:29,174
This poor boy is confused.

349
00:19:29,591 --> 00:19:32,010
We're just simple refugees.

350
00:19:32,386 --> 00:19:36,932
This young man wrecked my tea shop
and assaulted my employees!

351
00:19:37,015 --> 00:19:39,184
It's true, sir. We saw the whole thing.

352
00:19:39,267 --> 00:19:42,062
This crazy kid attacked
the finest tea maker in the city.

353
00:19:42,437 --> 00:19:44,940
Oh, that's very sweet.

354
00:19:46,066 --> 00:19:47,234
Come with us, son.

355
00:19:49,277 --> 00:19:50,404
( GRUNTING )

356
00:19:52,739 --> 00:19:53,782
You don't understand!

357
00:19:53,865 --> 00:19:55,075
They're Fire Nation!

358
00:19:55,158 --> 00:19:56,618
You have to believe me.

359
00:20:27,315 --> 00:20:28,942
Aang, the Earth King.

360
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,780
Greetings, your majesty.

361
00:20:33,905 --> 00:20:34,906
( GASPING )

362
00:20:41,997 --> 00:20:44,124
Augh, ugh, let me go!

363
00:20:47,377 --> 00:20:48,587
( MUFFLED SHOUT )

364
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:49,671
( MUFFLED SHOUT )

365
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,801
( CHIRPING )

366
00:20:57,053 --> 00:20:59,639
Avatar, it is a great honor to meet you.

367
00:20:59,723 --> 00:21:04,394
I am Long Feng, grand secretary
of Ba Sing Se and head of the Dai Li.

368
00:21:04,478 --> 00:21:05,729
I'd like to talk to you.

369
00:21:05,812 --> 00:21:08,231
Your friends will be
waiting for us in the library.

370
00:21:12,527 --> 00:21:14,738
SOKKA: Why won't you let us
talk to the king?

371
00:21:14,821 --> 00:21:17,741
We have information that could
defeat the Fire Nation!

372
00:21:17,824 --> 00:21:21,495
LONG FENG: The Earth King has no time
to get involved with political squabbles

373
00:21:21,578 --> 00:21:23,914
and the day-to-day minutia
of military activities.

374
00:21:23,997 --> 00:21:27,334
AANG: This could be the most
important thing he's ever heard.

375
00:21:27,417 --> 00:21:29,795
What's most important to his royal majesty

376
00:21:29,878 --> 00:21:33,256
is maintaining
the cultural heritage of Ba Sing Se.

377
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:36,426
All his duties relate to
issuing decrees on such matters.

378
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:41,640
It's my job to oversee the rest of the
city's resources, including the military.

379
00:21:41,973 --> 00:21:44,017
So the king is just a figurehead.

380
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:45,519
He's your puppet.

381
00:21:45,602 --> 00:21:47,479
Oh, no, no.

382
00:21:47,562 --> 00:21:50,982
His majesty is an icon,
a god to his people.

383
00:21:51,066 --> 00:21:54,861
He can't sully his hands
with the hourly changes of an endless war.

384
00:21:54,945 --> 00:21:56,780
But we found out about a solar eclipse

385
00:21:56,863 --> 00:21:58,949
that will leave
the Fire Nation defenseless.

386
00:21:59,032 --> 00:22:00,534
You could lead an invasion...

387
00:22:00,617 --> 00:22:02,994
Enough, I don't want to hear
your ridiculous plan.

388
00:22:03,078 --> 00:22:07,999
It is the strict policy of Ba Sing Se that
the war not be mentioned within the walls.

389
00:22:08,124 --> 00:22:10,168
Constant news of an escalating war

390
00:22:10,293 --> 00:22:13,255
will throw the citizens of Ba Sing Se
into a state of panic.

391
00:22:14,256 --> 00:22:16,341
You have to believe me,
they're firebenders.

392
00:22:16,424 --> 00:22:18,635
They won't stop until they win the war.

393
00:22:19,845 --> 00:22:22,264
Calm down, you're safe now.

394
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,352
Our economy would be ruined,

395
00:22:27,477 --> 00:22:30,230
our peaceful way of life,
our traditions would disappear.

396
00:22:31,356 --> 00:22:34,150
There's no war in Ba Sing Se.

397
00:22:34,818 --> 00:22:36,111
What are you talking about?

398
00:22:36,194 --> 00:22:39,281
Where do you think all the refugees
come from? You can't hide it.

399
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:45,120
In silencing talk of conflict, Ba Sing Se
remains a peaceful, orderly utopia.

400
00:22:45,662 --> 00:22:47,455
The last one on Earth.

401
00:22:48,874 --> 00:22:50,333
( MUFFLED GRUNTING )

402
00:22:51,001 --> 00:22:53,086
There is no war within the walls.

403
00:22:53,169 --> 00:22:54,462
Here we are safe.

404
00:22:55,213 --> 00:22:57,757
Here we are free.

405
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:02,137
You can't keep the truth
from all these people.

406
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:03,346
They have to know.

407
00:23:03,597 --> 00:23:04,806
I'll tell them.

408
00:23:04,890 --> 00:23:06,766
I'll make sure everyone knows.

409
00:23:06,850 --> 00:23:09,311
Until now, you've been treated
as our honored guest.

410
00:23:09,728 --> 00:23:13,565
But from now on, you will be
watched every moment by Dai Li agents.

411
00:23:13,690 --> 00:23:17,360
If you mention the war to anyone,
you will be expelled from the city.

412
00:23:17,736 --> 00:23:20,113
I understand you've been
looking for your bison.

413
00:23:20,196 --> 00:23:23,867
It would be quite a shame if you were
not able to complete your quest.

414
00:23:25,327 --> 00:23:27,871
Now Joo Dee will show you home.

415
00:23:30,206 --> 00:23:32,000
WOMAN: Come with me, please.

416
00:23:32,083 --> 00:23:33,376
What happened to Joo Dee?

417
00:23:33,835 --> 00:23:35,003
I'm Joo Dee.

418
00:23:35,086 --> 00:23:38,548
I'll be your host as long
as you're in our wonderful city.
